One issue: `ev.preventDefault()` on pointermove to prevent scrolling? Scrolling is controlled by touch-action. With touch-action:none on .disc-item, after a pointerdown on the item, the browser won't scroll. preventDefault on pointerdown (on the item) also prevents the mousedown defaults (text selection) — I'll set `e.preventDefault()` on pointerdown, but note: it prevents focus and click; no problem.

But the subtlety of pointerdown preventDefault: in some browsers it also prevents the compatible mouse events (mousedown), no problem. And on touch, does preventDefault on pointerdown stop touchstart? No — preventDefault on pointerdown does not cancel touchstart (touch events are separate). But touch-action:none handles it.

